jobDescription:
Job Description Role Overview: We are seeking a results-driven and analytical Industrial Engineer with experience in the aerospace manufacturing domain to drive continuous improvement across our production systems. The ideal candidate will have a solid background in process optimization, lean manufacturing, and resource planning within a high-precision engineering environment. Key

RESPONSIBILITIES:
• Analyze and optimize manufacturing workflows, production layouts, and material flow for efficiency and productivity. • Implement Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, and Kaizen practices to reduce waste and improve process capability. • Conduct time and motion studies to establish standard work procedures and labor utilization. • Collaborate with cross-functional teams (design, manufacturing, quality, and supply chain) to improve end-to-end operations. • Evaluate and improve plant layout, workstation design, and ergonomics to enhance safety and efficiency. • Develop and maintain production capacity models, analyze bottlenecks, and recommend process improvements. • Utilize tools such as VSM (Value Stream Mapping), PFMEA, and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) for process improvement initiatives. • Support the implementation of MES/ERP systems for real-time production monitoring and data analysis. • Drive cost reduction projects without compromising on quality or safety. • Prepare detailed process documentation, SOPs, and reports for continuous monitoring and auditing. Qualifications & Skills: • Bachelor’s or Master’s in Industrial Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or related field. • Minimum 4 years of industrial engineering experience, preferably in the aerospace or high-precision manufacturing industry. • Strong knowledge of lean tools, process optimization, and production systems. • Hands-on experience with CAD tools, ERP/MES systems, and data analysis tools (Excel, Power BI, etc.). • Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. • Familiarity with AS9100, NADCAP, or other aerospace quality standards is a plus. • Ability to work in a fast-paced, dynamic, and cross-disciplinary environment. I'm interested View all jobs Visit website Powered by {{criteria Index}} {{field}} {{captialize(condition)}} ( ) {{cx Prop Help Text}} {{cx Prop Field.consent_details.description}} {{record.Posting_Title}} {{record.Posting_Title}} {{record.Posting_Title}} {{candidate.Em